      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodbridge%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town center, known as Woodbridge Green, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places as a historic district.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodbridge%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Darling House Museum, once home to Yale tutor Thomas Darling, now preserves 18th‑century life and is on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodbridge%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Woodbridge’s library serves as a cultural hub, offering programs for all ages and hosting community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
